From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msscript.ocx: script control events, connection points, OLE object methods (3658)

msscript.ocx: script control events, connection points, OLE object methods

IConnectionPoint::Advise/Unadvise/EnumConnections and
IConnectionPointContainer::EnumConnectionPoints now work, so containers
can sink the DScriptControlSource Error event; the Error event fires from
IActiveScriptSite::OnScriptError after the Error object is filled, and
IOleControl::FreezeEvents suppresses it. IQuickActivate hooks up the
container's sinks and returns the control status. IActiveScriptSite::
GetItemInfo honours SCRIPTINFO_ITYPEINFO. IOleObject: SetHostNames, Close
(OnClose to advise sinks), DoVerb, EnumVerbs, Update, IsUpToDate,
GetUserClassID, GetUserType, SetExtent, Advise, Unadvise, EnumAdvise.
IPersistStreamInit::GetClassID/IsDirty.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 3081/3271 (fast-a): fast-a 3081 already implements the same connection points, Error event, IOleObject, IQuickActivate, FreezeEvents and persistence (a superset); 3658 is reduced to what 3081 lacks: IActiveScriptSite::GetItemInfo with SCRIPTINFO_ITYPEINFO, plus 3658's conformance tests (tests/msscript.c, sgcalls.c), which now run against 3081's implementation.
---
